{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Introduce juries to determine the facts in family courts",
        "additional_details": "Outdated stereotypes, stigma and expectations of how a \u201creal victim\u201d behaves can undermine fair assessments of abuse and we believe documented evidence is often overlooked in family courts, violating Article 6. We think scrutiny by a jury would ensure fair trials. The identity of participants should be protected and juries must be required to give reasoned findings. We think the government cannot credibly aim to halve violence against women and girls without addressing everyday harm within the family justice system.",
        "background": "Change the law so juries determine the facts in family courts in England and Wales. Juries should decide disputed facts on the balance of probabilities, with judges directing the law and deciding welfare outcomes. Require privacy safeguards and directions addressing trauma and victim stereotypes.",
